  "insights": [
   "August semiconductor shipment data from the SIA shows mostly above-seasonal trends, with integrated circuit units (ex-memory) increasing ~2% MoM.",
   "Overall shipments are now tracking 10% above long-term demand on a three-month moving average basis, up from 7% in July.",
   "Analog segment shipments are performing well, currently running ~10% above trend, an improvement from 6.5% above trend in July.",
   "Microcontroller (MCU) units remain a weak spot, tracking 21.3% below trend, similar to the 20.5% below-trend reading in July, likely due to consumer electronic softness.",
   "Memory segments showed strong revenue growth, with DRAM up 34% MoM and NAND up 41% MoM, both significantly outperforming typical seasonality.",
   "Goldman Sachs expects shipments to remain above trend in the medium term, citing the duration of below-trend shipments over the past four years and normalizing customer inventory levels.",
