  "title": "Global Technology: Reported HDD capacity additions by Toshiba: Framing implications for the HDD supply chain",
  "type": "sector",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-10-07",
  "insights": [
   "Toshiba intends to double nearline HDD production capacity by end of FY27 (March 2028) with a ~\u00a560 bn (~$380 mn) investment in its Philippines facility.",
   "Toshiba aims to triple its overall HDD market share to 30% from current ~11% and achieve mass production of 65 TB drives by 2030.",
   "Goldman Sachs notes Toshiba previously failed to meet similar ambitious expansion goals set at its 2022 Investor Day.",
   "STX and WDC are expected to maintain healthy pricing and margin dynamics despite Toshiba's expansion, as they hold a multi-generation technology advantage in HAMR.",
   "Toshiba's expansion could limit margin upside for STX and WDC in the medium term and potentially cap their equity multiples relative to the memory complex.",
   "The HDD components and materials supply chain is expected to benefit from increased volumes and higher product complexity, rather than suffering from intensified competition.",
   "Resonac's capacity expansion in Singapore is likely to be filled early by Toshiba, tightening supply/demand and increasing the likelihood of price hikes.",
