  "title": "Introducing the Option on Implied Dispersion",
  "type": "derivatives",
  "priority": "high",
  "published": "2026-10-07",
  "insights": [
   "Goldman Sachs is introducing a new product allowing clients to trade options on implied dispersion levels, removing the realized volatility component from the trade.",
   "The product allows for directional bets on the implied dispersion spread (the difference between single-stock volatility and index volatility) using a package of forward-starting straddles.",
   "The structure involves an option tenor (e.g., 3m) and a dispersion package tenor (e.g., 1y), with physical settlement into a straddle portfolio at maturity.",
   "This instrument provides a cleaner way to express views on correlation without the path-dependency of realized volatility, which has been a traditional hurdle in dispersion trading.",
   "The desk highlights that dispersion entry points reached all-time highs earlier in 2026, driving increased client interest in both long and reverse dispersion strategies.",
   "The pricing example provided for a 3m put on implied dispersion (3v lower strike) shows an upfront premium of $800,000 for a $1m vega-weighted basket."
