  "insights": [
   "Preliminary NFP releases are subject to significant estimation errors and seasonal noise, making them unreliable for literal interpretation.",
   "April and November initial NFP releases demonstrate the lowest mean absolute error (MAE) on a single-month basis, while January, September, March, and May show the largest revisions.",
   "On a 3-month moving average (3mma) basis, April, July, and October are the most reliable, whereas January, May, and September are the least reliable.",
   "Estimation biases in January and May tend to persist across months, meaning 3mma smoothing does little to reduce noise in these periods.",
   "Post-pandemic NFP releases have shifted from a historical underestimation bias to a common overstatement bias.",
